course: dictionary
lesson: 8770
title: Words with more than one job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning is right. The word sex is about being male or female. Look at the clues in this sentence: «Some children have two mums or two dads because their parents are a same-sex couple, and that family is just as real as any other.» Same-sex is about the two people in a couple, and sex here means male or female.
explain: Sex is a noun. You can talk about both sexes, meaning males and females together, or about a single-sex school, where all the pupils are boys or all are girls. A form may ask for your sex, and the answer is male or female.
explain: In science, sex is about biology. Animals and plants have male and female parts, and these help new living things to grow. If a word in a text makes you unsure, read the clues around it, and then ask a trusted adult.
fact: Sex means being male or female.
fact: Both sexes means males and females together.
fact: «Same-sex» means both people in a couple are the same sex, and such families are just as real as any other.
fact: Your body is private, and you should tell a trusted adult if anyone makes you feel uncomfortable.
fact: Sex is usually uncountable, but one of the two groups is called a sex, and both groups are sexes.
exercise: «Some children have two mums or two dads because their parents are a same-sex couple.» What does same-sex describe here? | *A couple where both people are male or both are female | A couple who live by the sea | A couple who are very old | A couple with one child
exercise: A form asks, «What is your sex?» What answer does it want? | Tall or short | *Male or female | Your favourite colour | Your birthday
exercise: Which phrase means males and females together? | *Both sexes | Sex education | Single-sex | Same-sex
test: In a science lesson, the teacher says, «Plants have male and female parts.» What does sex mean in that sentence? | Being happy or sad | Being very old | Being fast or slow | *Being male or female
test: «She goes to a single-sex school.» What does single-sex mean? | *All the pupils are boys, or all are girls | The school has no teachers | The pupils wear the same uniform | The school is near the sea
exam: If someone makes you feel uncomfortable about your body, what should you do? | Wait until you are older | Keep it secret forever | *Tell a trusted adult | Ignore it and hope it stops
